A||N||2||2xsess||A little tip for anyone with the lyin gas gauge problem||||1||
Z||000000||2xsess||01-28-2001||04:29 AM||||I got this out of Fiero Quarterly, it's a magazine that Tri-state Fiero Club used to publish. The Article was written by <BR>Mr. Joe Wynman. I've recently acquired 8 issues of the magazine from Joe, and they have some great info and tech stuff in them.<P>This is his helpful way to determine if it's the gauge causing wrong readings or the sending unit.<P>All Fieros have a three wire connector located in the engine compartment. Near the lower center of the firewall. This connector should be disconnected for this test.<BR>Using a straight length of wire short out terminals A and B on the connector, which is attached to the Fiero body harness. By performing this action you are simulating an empty tank. <B>Take extra caution to make sure you short the correct terminals. If you short the wrong ones you risk damaging your fuel level gauge or blowing the fuel pump fuse</B> Turn the ignition key to the run position, not the start position. If the gauge reads empty during this test but reads off during normal operation then the problem lies else where with in the calibration of the sending unit.<BR>A second test is used to determine the correct reading at full fuel level. Remove the wire you have shorting out A and B terminals and replace it with a 90 ohm resistor. <B>Again take caution in making sure you get it on the correct terminals.</B>Then turn the key to the "run" position and if the gauge reads full then the problem is in the calibration of your sending unit.<P>Whew, that was rahter long but I read a post somewhere that I wasn't the only one having this problem.<BR>If anyone thinks it's wrong for me to publish this here please say so and I'll remove it immediately. <P>Once again I give the credit to Joe Wynman of Associated Automotive, Hackensack, NJ<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||01-28-2001||08:23 AM||||I don't need it,but thanks for printing it.You can never have too much information.<BR>Thanks again ||||reg||1
